3. Third-party components
-------------------------

Third-party material redistributed in these artifacts is listed with its license
terms, copyright lines, and permission notices in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. That
file covers three kinds of source:

  * every package inlined into the built single-file bundle;
  * the inlined third-party code that is not an npm dependency (the Markdown
    parser bundled in the memory viewer template);
  * non-npm third-party expression shipped in the source tree — currently the
    external system prompts under src/agent/prompts/ that this fork collects for
    benchmarking. Those files originate with Anthropic's Claude Code (via the
    Piebald mirror), OpenAI's Codex CLI, and Google's Gemini CLI. They are
    third-party works reproduced for comparison; they are not this project's
    statements, and this project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or a
    product of any of those vendors.

That file is generated by scripts/generate-third-party-notices.cjs and must be
regenerated whenever dependencies change; the non-npm list it consumes lives in
scripts/non-npm-third-party-sources.json.


